From 6767c237a27f0fc5d38e504ba71b0aecb5b0757c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:25:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/15] S2-4b: the Fun Fair games compile for the PS1 again,
 with no resident byte added

The PS1 build (minigames are an overlay group there, the baked paths are compiled
out) broke on MgBox, unused names and implicit declarations after the stamp and band
work. MgBox is declared everywhere, the PS1 macros have void-cast stubs, MG_BAKED(f)
is NULL on the PS1, and the baked-only functions sit under #if !PS1.

mg_mod6 no longer keeps a 6-byte table (a static const in a minigame file lands in
the resident .data on the PS1): the Chinese remainder is r + 3 * ((x - r) & 1).
PS1 _end 0x801efe60 = the base, 64 KB left below the stack top with the boot FMV.

speed2_fair.txt: expect-fps 28 on every play window (Whack, Dodge, Gallery, Derby,
Memory, Catch). Core tests: 1115 passed, 0 failed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
